  "notes": "Fighting passage: only what the tafsirs say with their restrictions (the treaty-holders of that time, the four months, those who broke oaths and attacked); no battle, weapon, captive or killing drawn; no present-day reading. No motif on the Prophet ﷺ. 12:1-6 carries As-Sa'di's restriction (they broke their oaths by fighting you, helping others fight you, or diminishing you). Light for the prayer, hands for brotherhood, a book for «نفصل الآيات», a seal for the broken oaths. Al-Muyassar's first-person «ونبين الآيات» is not used. STAGING v4: Fighting and treaty passage: stays ambient (owner rule, Staging v4). The hands plate on 11:7 (du'a in the catalog) becomes a seal plate for the bond of brotherhood (as in Al-Anfal 72). The seal of the broken oaths (12:2) now leaves by undrawing. The background stays quiet on 11:10-11 (He details the verses)."
